	CS:group.AvFlightStatusGroup^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.badge.FlightTurnStatus^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:FlightTurnStatus^An aircraft turn takes on a status as follows:\&10\* Inbound \2013 The aircraft is scheduled to arrive at your location.\&10\* Arrived \2013 The aircraft has arrived at your location and the inbound flight for the turn has been completed.\&10\* In Maintenance \2013 The aircraft has arrived at the maintenance location, and the work package for the aircraft turn has been started.\&10\* Released \2013 The work package for the turn has been completed and the aircraft has been released to service.\&10\* Departed - The aircraft for the turn has taken off on the outbound flight.\&10\^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.LastReleaseDate^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:LastReleaseDate^Displays date and time in the time zone assigned to your airport. Click or hover over the time zone to see date and time in UTC.^
		CE:
	CE:
	CS:group.AvFlightWorkGroup^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.badge.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$RequestStateCd^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$RequestStateCd^A business entity takes on a status as follows:\&10\* SENT \2013 The business entity is in the process of being synchronized with an external service. \&10\* SUCCEEDED- The business entity has been successfully synchronized with the external service.\&10\* FAILED \2013 The synchronization of the business entity with the external service has failed.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$Barcode^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$Barcode^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$ConvertedDuration^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$ConvertedDuration^For work packages that are created as part of the workscope, this is the duration of the work package as specified in the workscope. For work packages that are created on packaging a fault to a new work package, the duration of the work package displays values based on the status of the aircraft turn, as follows:\&10\\&10\* For **Inbound** and **Arrived** turns, where the work package status is **Active** or **Committed**, the duration is zero.\&10\* For **In Maintenance** turns, where the work package status is **In Work**, the duration is zero.\&10\* For **Released** and **Departed** turns, where the work package status is **Completed**, the duration is the time in hours and minutes between the **Actual Start** and the **Actual End** of the work package.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$RequestCorrelationId^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$RequestCorrelationId^The ID used to track the communication for a given transaction. The Request Correlation ID correlates to the Correlation ID on the ***Communication Log*** page and can be used to look up the communication on the **Communication Log** page, to troubleshoot a communication error, if required.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^The work package number of the work package for the turn. A unique work package number is generated and displayed in this field for work packages loaded through the Workscope Loader or work packages created on packaging an open or deferred fault where no work package for the turn existed previously.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WorkPackageName^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WorkPackageName^^
		CE:
	CE:
