	CS:group.ReleaseStatus^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.field.CmsFailedWarnings^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:CmsFailedWarnings^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.CmsPendingWarnings^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:CmsPendingWarnings^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.HasNeardueFaults^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:HasNeardueFaults^Indicates if the aircraft has any near due faults.\&10\\&10\Near due faults are faults that have due dates falling within the time interval defined by the RELEASE_NOTIFY_INTERVAL parameter in Maintenix. \&10\\&10\A green **No** indicates that there are no near due faults for the aircraft in Maintenix.\&10\\&10\A yellow **Yes** indicates that there are near due faults for the aircraft in Maintenix.\&10\\&10\Click **Release Status Details** to view information about any near due faults.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.HasNeardueTasks^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:HasNeardueTasks^Indicates if the aircraft has any near due tasks.\&10\\&10\Near due tasks are tasks that have due dates falling within the time interval defined by the RELEASE_NOTIFY_INTERVAL parameter in Maintenix. \&10\\&10\A green **No** indicates that there are no near due tasks for the aircraft in Maintenix.\&10\\&10\A yellow **Yes** indicates that there are near due tasks for the aircraft in Maintenix.\&10\\&10\Click **Release Status Details** to view information about any near due tasks.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.HasOverdueFaults^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:HasOverdueFaults^Indicates if the aircraft has any overdue faults and if a hard stop is in effect.\&10\\&10\A green **No** indicates that there are no overdue faults in Maintenix   for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, and the same fault has not been closed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation. \&10\\&10\A yellow **Yes** indicates that there are overdue faults in Maintenix for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, the same fault has not been closed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation, and the \&10\RELEASE_OVERDUE_ FAULT parameter in Maintenix is set to WARN, with no hard stop in effect.\&10\\&10\A red **Yes** indicates that there are overdue faults in Maintenix for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, the same fault has not been completed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation, and the RELEASE_OVERDUE_ FAULT parameter in Maintenix is set to ERROR, with a hard stop in effect.\&10\\&10\Click **Release Status Details** to view information about any overdue faults. If a hard stop is in effect, you should package the overdue fault into a work package and then close it. If the fault is already in your work package, you should close or defer it or request a maintenance operations controller (MOC) to extend the deadline.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.HasOverdueTasks^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:HasOverdueTasks^Indicates if the aircraft has any overdue tasks and if a hard stop is in effect.\&10\\&10\A green **No** indicates that there are no overdue tasks in Maintenix   for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, and the same fault has not been closed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation.\&10\\&10\A green **Yes** indicates that there are overdue tasks in Maintenix for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, the same task has not been completed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation, and the RELEASE_OVERDUE_TASK parameter in Maintenix is set to OK.\&10\\&10\A yellow **Yes** indicates that there are overdue tasks in Maintenix for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, the same task has not been completed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation, and the RELEASE_OVERDUE_TASK parameter in Maintenix is set to WARN, with no hard stop in effect.\&10\\&10\A red **Yes** indicates that there are overdue tasks in Maintenix for the aircraft, for which the deadline has passed, the same task has not been completed in Mobile Maintenance for Aviation, and the RELEASE_OVERDUE_TASK parameter in Maintenix is set to ERROR, with a hard stop in effect.\&10\\&10\Click **Release Status Details** to view information about any overdue tasks.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.IsMandatoryComponentsMissing^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:IsMandatoryComponentsMissing^Indicates if the aircraft has any missing mandatory components and if a hard stop is in effect.\&10\\&10\A green **No** indicates that there are no missing mandatory components in the aircraft.\&10\\&10\A yellow **Yes** indicates that there are missing mandatory components in the aircraft and the RELEASE_MISSING_COMPONENT parameter in Maintenix is set to WARN, with no hard stop in effect.\&10\\&10\A red **Yes** indicates that there are missing mandatory components in the aircraft and the RELEASE_MISSING_COMPONENT parameter in Maintenix is set to ERROR, with a hard stop in effect. \&10\\&10\Click **Release Status Details** to view information about any missing mandatory components. If a hard stop is in effect, mandatory components must be installed before proceeding with the aircraft release.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.OpenFaultsStatus^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:OpenFaultsStatus^Indicates if the aircraft to be released has faults in **Open** status. Click **Release Status Details** to view details of any open faults. Open faults must be assigned to the work package and closed or deferred to release the aircraft.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.OpenTasksStatus^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:OpenTasksStatus^Indicates if the aircraft to be released has any tasks that are in the **Active** or **In Work** status on work package for the turn. Click **Release Status Details** to view details of any open tasks. Open tasks assigned to the work package for the turn must be completed to release the aircraft.^
		CE:
