	CS:group.AddPartsPartRequirement^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.field.IncludeInstallation^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:IncludeInstallation^Adds a part installation record. You cannot add another part installation requirement for the same position and configuration slot if a part installation record for that position and configuration slot already exists unless the existing part requirement has been signed off.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.IncludeRemoval^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:IncludeRemoval^Adds a part removal record. You cannot add another part removal requirement for the same position and configuration slot if a part removal record for that position and configuration slot already exists in the same work package.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.RemovalReasonRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:RemovalReasonRef^Select the part removal reason. If you do not select the part removal reason when adding a part, you need to select it when recording work for the part removal.^
		CE:
	CE:
	CS:group.AddResourceToolGroup^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.field.PartNo^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:PartNo^In this field you can indicate if you have a requirement for a specific Part Number of the Tool/Equipment required to resolve the fault. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter a part and serial number or directly select a specific Tool/Equipment. Note that it is not mandatory for Tool/Equipment objects to have a reference to a Part Number.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.SchedDuration^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:SchedDuration^This will indicate the time that the Tool/Equipment is scheduled to be used to resolve the fault. The Scheduled Hours is entered in the format HH:MM (i.e. 02:30 represents 2 hours and 30 minutes). The Scheduled Hours will be used in resource management to analyze the availability and allocate tools to work tasks.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.SerialNo^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:SerialNo^In this field you can indicate if you have a requirement for a specific Serial Number of the Tool/Equipment required to resolve the fault. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter a part and serial number or directly select a specific Tool/Equipment. Note that it is not mandatory for Tool/Equipment objects to have a reference to a Serial Number.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.ResourceGroupIdRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ResourceGroupIdRef^The ID of the Tool/Equipment Group that includes the Tool/Equipment needed to resolve the fault. Tools/Equipment Groups are defined in the resource group in the ***Resource Details*** page using the type **Tool/Equipment Group**. Only groups set up to be used in maintenance will be available for FLM faults.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.ResourceIdRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ResourceIdRef^The specific Tool/Equipment required to resolve the fault. Tools/Equipment are defined in the ***Tool/Equipment*** page and is also available as a Resource in the Resource Management area.^
		CE:
	CE:
