			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$ExternalId^A reference number that is used to refer to an external system. If a record has been received from another system, the original identity is saved as an external identity. You can also enter a non-unique alphanumeric value in this field, which can be edited later on^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^The work package planned for an aircraft turn is displayed as follows:\&10\* For aircraft turns in the Inbound or Arrived status where a departure flight has been linked, the earliest of the work packages with Scheduled Start on or after the Scheduled Arrival of the arrival flight and before the Scheduled Departure of the departure flight is displayed. When a departure flight has not been linked for an aircraft turn, the earliest of the work packages with Scheduled Start on or after the Scheduled Arrival of the arrival flight is displayed.\&10\* For aircraft turns in the In Maintenance status, the work package with the latest Actual Start is displayed.\&10\* For aircraft turns in the Released and Departed status, the work package with the latest Actual End after the Actual Arrival of the flight is displayed. \&10\^
		CE:
