CS:FlmResourceAllocationGant^WEB^Global Data^N^N
	CS:group.AvResourceToolEquipmentTaskGroup^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.field.AircraftTypeName^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AircraftTypeName^The combination of aircraft description and registration code. You can search for and enter an aircraft in this field using the aircraft registration code or tail number.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^ The work package to which the task has been assigned.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.Priority^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:Priority^The classification that differentiates tasks based on their urgency. Organizations can define their own priority levels.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.RecordId^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:RecordId^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.SchedEndDateTime^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:SchedEndDateTime^The date and time at which the work package is scheduled to end. Displays date and time in the time zone assigned to your airport. Click or hover over the time zone to see date and time in UTC.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.SchedStartDateTime^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:SchedStartDateTime^The date and time at which the work package is scheduled to start. Displays date and time in the time zone assigned to your airport. Click or hover over the time zone to see date and time in UTC.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.TaskCode^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:TaskCode^The task code is the code assigned to the task definition, and for actual tasks based on task definitions, the task code is the first part of the name of the task. For ad hoc tasks, the task name is its code.^
		CE:
	CE:
	CS:group.AvResourceToolEquipmentToolGroup^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.field.PartNo^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:PartNo^This field indicates the Part Number of the Tool/Equipment required to perform the work task. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter a part and serial number or directly select a specific Tool/Equipment. Note that it is not mandatory for Tool/Equipment objects to have a reference to a Part Number. If the tool usage is signed off, this field will indicate the actual Part No used when completing the task.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.ScheduleTime^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ScheduleTime^This will indicate the time that the Tool/Equipment is scheduled to be used to resolve the work task. The Scheduled Hours is entered in the format HH:MM (i.e. 02:30 represents 2 hours and 30 minutes). The Scheduled Hours will be used in resource management to analyze the availability and allocate tools to work tasks.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.SerialNo^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:SerialNo^This field indicates the Serial Number of the Tool/Equipment required to resolve the work task. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter a part and serial number or directly select a specific Tool/Equipment. Note that it is not mandatory for Tool/Equipment objects to have a reference to a Serial Number. If the tool usage is signed off, this field will indicate the Serial No used when completing the task.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.ResourceGroupIdRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ResourceGroupIdRef^The ID of the Tool/Equipment Group that includes the Tool/Equipment needed to resolve the work task. Tools/Equipment Groups are defined in the resource group in the ***Resource Details*** page using the type **Tool/Equipment Group**. Only groups set up to be used in maintenance will be available for FLM work tasks.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.ResourceIdRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ResourceIdRef^The specific Tool/Equipment required to resolve the work task. Tools/Equipment are defined in the ***Tool/Equipment*** page and is also available as a Resource in the Resource Management area.^
		CE:
	CE:
