	CS:list.TurnsList^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:listcontent.badge.FlightTurnStatus^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:FlightTurnStatus^An aircraft turn takes on a status as follows:\&10\* Inbound \2013 The aircraft is scheduled to arrive at your location.\&10\* Arrived \2013 The aircraft has arrived at your location and the inbound flight for the turn has been completed.\&10\* In Maintenance \2013 The aircraft has arrived at the maintenance location, and the work package for the aircraft turn has been started.\&10\* Released \2013 The work package for the turn has been completed and the aircraft has been released to service.\&10\* Departed - The aircraft for the turn has taken off on the outbound flight.^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.ActualArrivalDateTime^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ActualArrivalDateTime^Displays date and time in the time zone assigned to your airport. Click or hover over the time zone to see date and time in UTC.^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.ActualOutboundDeptDateTime^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ActualOutboundDeptDateTime^Displays date and time in the time zone assigned to your airport. Click or hover over the time zone to see date and time in UTC.^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AircraftRef$RegCode^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AircraftRef$RegCode^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.ArrivalGate^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ArrivalGate^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$ExternalId^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$ExternalId^A reference number that is used to refer to an external system. If a record has been received from another system, the original identity is saved as an external identity. You can also enter a non-unique alphanumeric value in this field, which can be edited later on^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^The work package planned for an aircraft turn is displayed as follows:\&10\* For aircraft turns in the Inbound or Arrived status where a departure flight has been linked, the earliest of the work packages with Scheduled Start on or after the Scheduled Arrival of the arrival flight and before the Scheduled Departure of the departure flight is displayed. When a departure flight has not been linked for an aircraft turn, the earliest of the work packages with Scheduled Start on or after the Scheduled Arrival of the arrival flight is displayed.\&10\* For aircraft turns in the In Maintenance status, the work package with the latest Actual Start is displayed.\&10\* For aircraft turns in the Released and Departed status, the work package with the latest Actual End after the Actual Arrival of the flight is displayed.^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvAirportRef$IataCode^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAirportRef$IataCode^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvAssemblyRef$AssemblyTypeName^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAssemblyRef$AssemblyTypeName^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvFlightDepartureRef$DepartureGate^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvFlightDepartureRef$DepartureGate^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.AvFlightDepartureRef$LegNo^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvFlightDepartureRef$LegNo^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.GroundTime^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:GroundTime^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.LegNo^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:LegNo^^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.NoOfAssignedTasks^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:NoOfAssignedTasks^Number of Tasks in the Work Package.^
		CE:
		CS:listcontent.field.TotalHours^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:TotalHours^Total labour hours required for the Work Package connected to the Turn.^
		CE:
	CE:
CE:
