	CS:group.AvExeTaskGroup^WEB^Global Data^N^N
		CS:groupcontent.badge.Objstate^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:Objstate^A task has one of the following statuses:\&10\* **Active**- The task was created but has not started.\&10\* **In Work**-The task was started.\&10\* **Complete**- The task was completed.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.badge.OverallAssignmentsProgress^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:OverallAssignmentsProgress^Displays the overall status of skill assignments within the task.\&10\\&10\* Not Started \2013 All assignments are either assigned or unassigned.\&10\* In Progress \2013 At least one assignment is in the **Work Started** status.\&10\* Paused \2013 Some assignments are completed, while others are assigned or unassigned.\&10\* Finished \2013 All assignments are completed.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.badge.OverallPanelStatus^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:OverallPanelStatus^Status of an individual panel of a maintenance, MPC Open, or MPC Close task. Possible statuses are **To Be Opened**, **Opened**, **Ready To Close**, **Closed**, or **No MPC**.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.badge.RequestStateCd^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:RequestStateCd^A business entity takes on a status as follows:\&10\* SENT \2013 The business entity is in the process of being synchronized with an external service. \&10\* SUCCEEDED- The business entity has been successfully synchronized with the external service.\&10\* FAILED \2013 The synchronization of the business entity with the external service has failed.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.badge.Sensitivities^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:Sensitivities^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.ActualFinish^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ActualFinish^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AssemblyTypeName^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AssemblyTypeName^^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.field.AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:AvAircraftWorkPackageRef$WoNumber^The work package number of the work package for the turn. A unique work package number is generated and displayed in this field for work packages loaded through the Workscope Loader or work packages created on packaging an open or deferred fault where no work package for the turn existed previously.^
		CE:
