		CS:groupcontent.field.ActualDuration^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ActualDuration^The actual time that the Tool/Equipment was used to perform the work task. The Actual Hours must be entered in the format HH:MM (i.e. 02:30 represents 2 hours and 30 minutes).^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.PartCatalogRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:PartCatalogRef^This field indicates the Part Number of the Tool/Equipment used to perform the work task. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter a part and serial number or directly select a specific Tool/Equipment. Note that it is not mandatory for Tool/Equipment objects to have a reference to a Part Number.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.PartSerialCatalogRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:PartSerialCatalogRef^This field indicates the Serial Number of the Tool/Equipment used to resolve the work task. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter a part and serial number or directly select a specific Tool/Equipment. Note that it is not mandatory for Tool/Equipment objects to have a reference to a Serial Number.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.ResourceGroupIdRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ResourceGroupIdRef^The ID of the Tool/Equipment Group that includes the Tool/Equipment needed to resolve the work task. Tools/Equipment Groups are defined in the resource group in the ***Resource Details*** page using the type **Tool/Equipment Group**. Only groups set up to be used in maintenance will be available for FLM work tasks.^
		CE:
		CS:groupcontent.lookup.ResourceIdRef^WEB^Data Field^N^N
			D:ResourceIdRef^This field indicates the specific Tool/Equipment used to perform the work task. Tools/Equipment are defined in the ***Tool/Equipment*** page and is also available as a Resource in the Resource Management area. To identify the specific tool used you can either enter the Tool/Equipment or a part and serial number that represents a specific Tool/Equipment.^
		CE:
	CE:
